  "Question": "The factors of the expression \\(x^2+y^2\\) are:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\((x+y)(x-y)\\)",
    "B": "\\((x+y)^2\\)",
    "C": "\\((x^{\\frac{2}{3}}+y^{\\frac{2}{3}})(x^{\\frac{4}{3}}+y^{\\frac{4}{3}})\\)",
    "D": "\\((x+iy)(x-iy)\\)",
    "E": "none of these"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "The complex number \\(i\\) satisfies \\(i^2=-1\\), so \\((iy)^2=-y^2\\). This lets us write the sum of squares as a difference of squares and factor:\n\\[\nx^2+y^2=x^2-(iy)^2=(x+iy)(x-iy).\n\\]\nThese are factors over the complex numbers, as allowed by the displayed choices. The answer is D.",
